# 必考词 Unit05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit05核心词汇

{{gain}}{{/ɡeɪn}}{{v./n. 获得；增加；收益}}{{She gained valuable experience from the internship.}}
{{gap}}{{/ɡæp}}{{n. 缺口；差距；间隔}}{{There is a significant gap between the rich and the poor.}}
{{gather}}{{/ˈɡæðər}}{{v. 聚集；收集；推断}}{{People gathered in the square to celebrate the festival.}}
{{gaze}}{{/ɡeɪz}}{{v./n. 凝视；注视}}{{She gazed at the stars in the night sky.}}
{{gender}}{{/ˈdʒendər}}{{n. 性别}}{{Gender equality is an important social issue.}}
{{gene}}{{/dʒiːn}}{{n. 基因}}{{Genes play a key role in determining physical traits.}}
{{generate}}{{/ˈdʒenəreɪt}}{{v. 产生；引起}}{{The wind turbines generate electricity for the town.}}
{{generous}}{{/ˈdʒenərəs}}{{adj. 慷慨的；大方的；丰富的}}{{She is generous with her time and money.}}
{{genetic}}{{/dʒəˈnetɪk}}{{adj. 遗传的；基因的}}{{Genetic testing can reveal potential health risks.}}
{{genius}}{{/ˈdʒiːniəs}}{{n. 天才；天赋}}{{Einstein was a genius in physics.}}
{{genuine}}{{/ˈdʒenjuɪn}}{{adj. 真正的；真诚的}}{{The painting is a genuine masterpiece.}}
{{gesture}}{{/ˈdʒestʃər}}{{n./v. 手势；姿态；表示}}{{He made a gesture of welcome with his hand.}}
{{global}}{{/ˈɡləʊbl}}{{adj. 全球的；全面的}}{{Global warming is a major environmental concern.}}
{{glory}}{{/ˈɡlɔːri}}{{n. 光荣；荣耀；壮丽}}{{The athletes brought glory to their country.}}
{{glow}}{{/ɡləʊ}}{{v./n. 发光；发热；光辉}}{{The campfire glowed in the darkness.}}
{{goal}}{{/ɡəʊl}}{{n. 目标；进球；球门}}{{Her goal is to become a successful writer.}}
{{govern}}{{/ˈɡʌvn}}{{v. 统治；管理；支配}}{{The country is governed by a democratic system.}}
{{grace}}{{/ɡreɪs}}{{n. 优雅；恩惠；风度}}{{She moved with grace and elegance.}}
{{gradual}}{{/ˈɡrædʒuəl}}{{adj. 逐渐的；渐进的}}{{There has been a gradual improvement in his health.}}
{{grant}}{{/ɡrɑːnt}}{{v./n. 授予；拨款；助学金}}{{The government granted permission for the construction.}}
{{graphic}}{{/ˈɡræfɪk}}{{adj. 图形的；生动的；形象的}}{{The report includes graphic illustrations of the data.}}
{{grasp}}{{/ɡrɑːsp}}{{v./n. 抓住；理解；掌握；领悟}}{{He quickly grasped the main idea of the article.}}
{{grateful}}{{/ˈɡreɪtfl}}{{adj. 感激的；感谢的}}{{I am grateful for your generous help.}}
{{grave}}{{/ɡreɪv}}{{adj./n. 严重的；坟墓；严肃的}}{{The patient is in a grave condition.}}
{{gravity}}{{/ˈɡrævəti}}{{n. 重力；严重性；严肃}}{{Gravity keeps us firmly on the ground.}}
{{grieve}}{{/ɡriːv}}{{v. 使悲伤；哀悼；伤心}}{{She grieved the loss of her beloved pet.}}
{{grip}}{{/ɡrɪp}}{{v./n. 紧握；控制；理解}}{{He gripped the rope tightly to avoid falling.}}
{{gross}}{{/ɡrəʊs}}{{adj./n. 总的；严重的；毛额；总额}}{{The gross profit of the company increased by 15%.}}
{{guarantee}}{{/ˌɡærənˈtiː}}{{v./n. 保证；担保；保修}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}
{{guide}}{{/ɡaɪd}}{{n./v. 导游；指导；指南}}{{The guide led us through the ancient temple.}}
{{guilty}}{{/ˈɡɪlti}}{{adj. 有罪的；内疚的；有过失的}}{{He was found guilty of theft.}}
{{halt}}{{/hɔːlt}}{{v./n. 停止；暂停；中断}}{{The train came to a halt at the station.}}
{{hamper}}{{/ˈhæmpər}}{{v. 妨碍；阻碍；束缚}}{{Bad weather hampered the rescue operation.}}
{{handle}}{{/ˈhændl}}{{v./n. 处理；把手；操纵}}{{She handles pressure very well.}}
{{harbor}}{{/ˈhɑːbər}}{{n./v. 港口；怀有；庇护}}{{The ship arrived at the harbor early in the morning.}}
{{hardship}}{{/ˈhɑːdʃɪp}}{{n. 艰难；困苦；苦难}}{{They endured many hardships during the war.}}
{{harm}}{{/hɑːm}}{{n./v. 伤害；损害；危害}}{{Smoking does great harm to your health.}}
{{harmony}}{{/ˈhɑːməni}}{{n. 和谐；协调；融洽}}{{The community lives in harmony with nature.}}
{{harsh}}{{/hɑːʃ}}{{adj. 严厉的；恶劣的；刺耳的}}{{The harsh winter made travel difficult.}}
{{harvest}}{{/ˈhɑːvɪst}}{{n./v. 收获；收割；成果}}{{The farmers celebrated a good harvest this year.}}
{{haste}}{{/heɪst}}{{n. 匆忙；急忙；草率}}{{In her haste, she forgot to lock the door.}}
{{hatred}}{{/ˈheɪtrɪd}}{{n. 憎恨；仇恨；敌意}}{{Hatred only breeds more hatred.}}
{{haunt}}{{/hɔːnt}}{{v./n. 常去；萦绕；鬼魂出没}}{{The memory of the accident still haunts her.}}
{{heal}}{{/hiːl}}{{v. 治愈；痊愈；和解}}{{The wound took a long time to heal.}}
{{hesitate}}{{/ˈhezɪteɪt}}{{v. 犹豫；踌躇；不愿意}}{{Don't hesitate to ask if you need help.}}
{{highlight}}{{/ˈhaɪlaɪt}}{{v./n. 强调；亮点；最精彩部分}}{{The report highlights the importance of education.}}
{{hinder}}{{/ˈhɪndər}}{{v. 阻碍；妨碍；耽搁">{{Bad weather hindered the construction progress.}}
{{hint}}{{/hɪnt}}{{n./v. 暗示；提示；线索}}{{She gave me a hint about the answer.}}
{{honor}}{{/ˈɒnər}}{{n./v. 荣誉；尊敬；给予荣誉}}{{It is an honor to receive this award.}}
{{horizon}}{{/həˈraɪzn}}{{n. 地平线；视野；范围}}{{The sun disappeared below the horizon.}}
{{host}}{{/həʊst}}{{n./v. 主人；主持；招待；主办}}{{She hosted a dinner party for her friends.}}
{{household}}{{/ˈhaʊshəʊld}}{{n./adj. 家庭；家用的；家喻户晓的}}{{Household expenses have increased this year.}}
{{humble}}{{/ˈhʌmbl}}{{adj. 谦虚的；卑微的；简陋的}}{{Despite his success, he remains humble.}}
{{hypothesis}}{{/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs}}{{n. 假设；假说；前提}}{{The scientist tested the hypothesis through experiments.}}
{{identical}}{{/aɪˈdentɪkl}}{{adj. 完全相同的；同一的}}{{The two paintings look almost identical.}}
{{identify}}{{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ}}{{v. 识别；确认；鉴定}}{{The witness identified the suspect in court.}}
{{ideology}}{{/ˌaɪdiˈɒlədʒi}}{{n. 意识形态；思想体系}}{{Political ideology influences policy decisions.}}
{{ignorant}}{{/ˈɪɡnərənt}}{{adj. 无知的；愚昧的；不了解的}}{{He was ignorant of the risks involved.}}
{{ignore}}{{/ɪɡˈnɔːr}}{{v. 忽视；不理睬；忽略}}{{He ignored the warning signs and continued driving.}}
{{illuminate}}{{/ɪˈluːmɪneɪt}}{{v. 照亮；阐明；启发}}{{The study illuminates the relationship between diet and health.}}
{{illustrate}}{{/ˈɪləstreɪt}}{{v. 说明；插图；举例说明}}{{The diagram illustrates the process of photosynthesis.}}
{{image}}{{/ˈɪmɪdʒ}}{{n. 图像；形象；印象}}{{The company is trying to improve its public image.}}
{{immerse}}{{/ɪˈmɜːs}}{{v. 浸入；沉浸于；使专心于}}{{She immersed herself in the study of ancient history.}}
{{immune}}{{/ɪˈmjuːn}}{{adj. 免疫的；不受影响的；豁免的}}{{The vaccine makes you immune to the disease.}}
{{impact}}{{/ˈɪmpækt}}{{n./v. 影响；冲击；撞击}}{{The new policy will have a significant impact on education.}}
{{impair}}{{/ɪmˈpeər}}{{v. 损害；削弱；减少}}{{Loud noise can impair your hearing.}}
{{impart}}{{/ɪmˈpɑːt}}{{v. 传授；给予；告知}}{{The teacher imparted knowledge to the students.}}
{{implement}}{{/ˈɪmplɪment}}{{v./n. 实施；工具；手段}}{{The government plans to implement the new policy next year.}}
{{implication}}{{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 含义；暗示；影响；牵连}}{{The findings have important implications for future research.}}
{{implicit}}{{/ɪmˈplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 含蓄的；暗示的；无疑问的}}{{There was an implicit understanding between them.}}
{{imply}}{{/ɪmˈplaɪ}}{{v. 暗示；意味着；说明}}{{His silence implied agreement with the proposal.}}
{{impose}}{{/ɪmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 强加；征收；利用}}{{The government imposed a tax on luxury goods.}}
{{impulse}}{{/ˈɪmpʌls}}{{n. 冲动；脉冲；推动力}}{{She bought the dress on impulse.}}
{{incentive}}{{/ɪnˈsentɪv}}{{n. 激励；动机；刺激}}{{The company offers bonuses as an incentive for good performance.}}
{{incline}}{{/ɪnˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 倾向；斜面；倾斜}}{{I am inclined to agree with your suggestion.}}
{{incorporate}}{{/ɪnˈkɔːpəreɪt}}{{v. 包含；合并；组成公司}}{{The new design incorporates the latest technology.}}
{{incredible}}{{/ɪnˈkredəbl}}{{adj. 难以置信的；惊人的}}{{The view from the top was incredible.}}
{{index}}{{/ˈɪndeks}}{{n. 索引；指数；指标}}{{The stock market index rose by 2% today.}}
{{indicate}}{{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt}}{{v. 表明；指示；象征}}{{The data indicates a positive trend.}}
{{indifferent}}{{/ɪnˈdɪfərənt}}{{adj. 漠不关心的；中等的；一般的}}{{He seemed indifferent to the outcome of the election.}}
{{indignant}}{{/ɪnˈdɪɡnənt}}{{adj. 愤慨的；义愤的}}{{She was indignant at the unfair treatment.}}
{{indispensable}}{{/ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl}}{{adj. 不可缺少的；必需的}}{{Water is indispensable for life.}}
{{individual}}{{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl}}{{adj./n. 个人的；个体；个人}}{{Each individual has the right to express their opinion.}}
{{induce}}{{/ɪnˈdjuːs}}{{v. 引起；诱导；导致}}{{Stress can induce various health problems.}}
{{indulge}}{{/ɪnˈdʌldʒ}}{{v. 沉溺；放纵；纵容}}{{She indulged in her favorite hobby on weekends.}}
{{industry}}{{/ˈɪndəstri}}{{n. 工业；行业；勤勉}}{{The tourism industry is a major source of income.}}
{{inevitable}}{{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl}}{{adj. 不可避免的；必然的}}{{Change is inevitable in a rapidly developing world.}}
{{infer}}{{/ɪnˈfɜːr}}{{v. 推断；推论；暗示}}{{We can infer from the data that sales are improving.}}
{{inferior}}{{/ɪnˈfɪəriər}}{{adj./n. 低等的；下级的；次品}}{{The product was of inferior quality.}}
{{inflate}}{{/ɪnˈfleɪt}}{{v. 使膨胀；使通货膨胀；夸大}}{{The balloon inflated quickly.}}
{{inflation}}{{/ɪnˈfleɪʃn}}{{n. 通货膨胀；膨胀；夸大}}{{High inflation reduces the purchasing power of consumers.}}
{{influence}}{{/ˈɪnfluəns}}{{n./v. 影响；感化；势力}}{{Social media has a great influence on young people.}}
{{inform}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːm}}{{v. 通知；告知；了解}}{{Please inform us of any changes to the schedule.}}
{{ingredient}}{{/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt}}{{n. 成分；原料；因素}}{{Fresh ingredients make the food taste better.}}
{{inhabit}}{{/ɪnˈhæbɪt}}{{v. 居住于；栖息于}}{{Many species inhabit the tropical rainforest.}}
{{inherent}}{{/ɪnˈhɪərənt}}{{adj. 固有的；内在的；天生的}}{{There are inherent risks in any investment.}}
{{inherit}}{{/ɪnˈherɪt}}{{v. 继承；遗传；从前任接过}}{{She inherited a large fortune from her grandfather.}}
{{initial}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃl}}{{adj./n. 最初的；首字母；开始}}{{The initial results of the study are promising.}}
{{initiate}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃieɪt}}{{v. 开始；发起；使入门}}{{The company initiated a new training program.}}
{{initiative}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv}}{{n. 主动性；倡议；新方案}}{{She took the initiative to organize the event.}}
{{innocent}}{{/ˈɪnəsnt}}{{adj. 无辜的；天真的；无害的}}{{The jury found the defendant innocent.}}
{{innovation}}{{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn}}{{n. 创新；革新；新事物}}{{Innovation is the key to business success.}}
{{input}}{{/ˈɪnpʊt}}{{n./v. 输入；投入；信息}}{{We need more input from the team before making a decision.}}
{{inquire}}{{/ɪnˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 询问；调查；查究}}{{She inquired about the price of the item.}}
{{insight}}{{/ˈɪnsaɪt}}{{n. 洞察力；见解；深刻理解}}{{The book provides valuable insights into human behavior.}}
{{inspect}}{{/ɪnˈspekt}}{{v. 检查；视察；审视}}{{Health inspectors inspect restaurants regularly.}}
{{inspire}}{{/ɪnˈspaɪər}}{{v. 激励；启发；鼓舞}}{{Her speech inspired many young people to pursue their dreams.}}
{{install}}{{/ɪnˈstɔːl}}{{v. 安装；设置；就职}}{{They installed a new air conditioning system.}}
{{instance}}{{/ˈɪnstəns}}{{n. 例子；实例；场合}}{{For instance, you could try a different approach.}}
{{instant}}{{/ˈɪnstənt}}{{adj./n. 立即的；瞬间；即时}}{{The medicine provides instant relief from pain.}}
{{instinct}}{{/ˈɪnstɪŋkt}}{{n. 本能；直觉；天性}}{{Animals rely on instinct to find food.}}
{{institute}}{{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt}}{{n./v. 学院；制定；建立}}{{The research institute published a groundbreaking study.}}
{{institution}}{{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn}}{{n. 机构；制度；习俗}}{{Universities are important educational institutions.}}
{{instruct}}{{/ɪnˈstrʌkt}}{{v. 指导；命令；教授}}{{The teacher instructed the students to open their books.}}
{{instrument}}{{/ˈɪnstrəmənt}}{{n. 仪器；乐器；手段}}{{She plays several musical instruments.}}
{{insurance}}{{/ɪnˈʃʊərəns}}{{n. 保险；保险费；保障}}{{Health insurance covers most medical expenses.}}
{{integrate}}{{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt}}{{v. 整合；使融合；使完整}}{{The company integrated the new system into its operations.}}
{{intellectual}}{{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl}}{{adj./n. 智力的；知识分子}}{{Intellectual property is protected by law.}}
{{intelligence}}{{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns}}{{n. 智力；情报；智能}}{{Artificial intelligence is advancing rapidly.}}
{{intend}}{{/ɪnˈtend}}{{v. 打算；想要；意指}}{{We intend to finish the project by December.}}
{{intense}}{{/ɪnˈtens}}{{adj. 强烈的；紧张的；热烈的}}{{The competition was intense.}}
{{intention}}{{/ɪnˈtenʃn}}{{n. 意图；目的；打算}}{{He had no intention of leaving the company.}}
{{interact}}{{/ˌɪntərˈækt}}{{v. 互动；相互作用；交流}}{{Children learn by interacting with their peers.}}
{{interfere}}{{/ˌɪntəˈfɪər}}{{v. 干涉；妨碍；干扰}}{{Please do not interfere with my work.}}
{{internal}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːnl}}{{adj. 内部的；国内的；体内的}}{{The company resolved its internal conflicts.}}
{{interpret}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt}}{{v. 解释；口译；理解}}{{Different people may interpret the poem differently.}}
{{interrupt}}{{/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt}}{{v. 打断；中断；妨碍}}{{It is rude to interrupt someone while they are speaking.}}
{{interval}}{{/ˈɪntəvl}}{{n. 间隔；休息时间；间距}}{{The buses run at 15-minute intervals.}}
{{intervene}}{{/ˌɪntəˈviːn}}{{v. 干预；介入；调停}}{{The government intervened to stabilize the economy.}}
{{intimate}}{{/ˈɪntɪmət}}{{adj. 亲密的；私人的；详尽的}}{{They have been intimate friends for years.}}
{{intricate}}{{/ˈɪntrɪkət}}{{adj. 复杂的；精细的；错综的}}{{The watch has an intricate mechanism.}}
{{intrinsic}}{{/ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk}}{{adj. 内在的；固有的；本质的}}{{The intrinsic value of the painting is immeasurable.}}
{{invade}}{{/ɪnˈveɪd}}{{v. 入侵；侵犯；涌入}}{{The army invaded the neighboring country.}}
{{investigate}}{{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 调查；研究；审查}}{{The police are investigating the cause of the fire.}}
{{invest}}{{/ɪnˈvest}}{{v. 投资；投入；授予}}{{She invested a large sum in the stock market.}}
{{invisible}}{{/ɪnˈvɪzəbl}}{{adj. 看不见的；无形的；不露面的}}{{The air around us is invisible.}}
{{involve}}{{/ɪnˈvɒlv}}{{v. 涉及；包含；使参与}}{{The project involves a lot of teamwork.}}
{{isolate}}{{/ˈaɪsəleɪt}}{{v. 隔离；孤立；使分离}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of disease.}}
{{issue}}{{/ˈɪʃuː}}{{n./v. 问题；发行；发布；流出}}{{Climate change is a global issue.}}
{{justify}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ}}{{v. 证明…正当；为…辩护；证明…有道理}}{{How can you justify spending so much money?}}
